<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav October industry output rises 15.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav October industry output rises 15.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT  OCT 96     SEPT 96     OCT 95</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	    + 15.4	+  6.9	 n.a.</p>
<p> change yr/yr		    + 12.6	+  9.7	 n.a.</p>
<p> index (base average 1995)    126.9	 109.4	 n.a.</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE DATA (JAN TO OCT)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		+  6.5	+  5.6	 n.a.</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1995)    109.8	 110.6	 n.a.</p>
<p>NOTES - Industrial output in October 1996 was 38.2 percent, down from the same month in 1991.</p>
<p>Cummulative January-October 1996 output was 45.6 percent below the same period in 1991.</p>
<p>Data largely exclude the private sector, where manufacturing is not significant. Data cover rump Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
